WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:19.181
and Grildig," the king said one day, "we are going to a town near the south coast."

2
00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.202
"That's wonderful," I replied.

3
00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.522
"I'd like to see the sea again."

4
00:00:25.142 --> 00:00:27.043
We reached the town a few days later.

5
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:32.761
The next morning Glumdalclitch said to me, "I'm not feeling well.

6
00:00:33.942 --> 00:00:37.085
One of the queen's servants will look after you today."

7
00:00:38.206 --> 00:00:40.247
I asked the servant to take me to the sea.

8
00:00:40.988 --> 00:00:44.571
He carried me in my traveling box to a cliff above the shore.

9
00:00:44.591 --> 00:00:50.155
"I'll be back in half an hour," he said, and went to look for birds' eggs.

10
00:00:50.936 --> 00:00:55.079
The day was warm and I fell asleep in my box, listening to the waves.

11
00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.684
I woke up because my box was moving and I was being thrown around inside it.

12
00:01:01.504 --> 00:01:02.684
I was very afraid.

13
00:01:03.745 --> 00:01:09.386
I could feel the box rising high up into the air, but I could not understand why that

14
00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:10.147
was happening.

15
00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:13.727
Soon the land and sea were far below me.

16
00:01:14.388 --> 00:01:19.109
I could hear a noise over my head that sounded like the flapping of a bird's wings.

17
00:01:20.309 --> 00:01:23.990
A large bird had picked up my box and was flying away with it!

18
00:01:24.791 --> 00:01:26.851
Suddenly, the bird dropped the box.

19
00:01:27.471 --> 00:01:29.872
With a loud splash, it hit the water.

20
00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.362
Luckily, the windows were shut and kept the water out.

21
00:01:34.282 --> 00:01:37.604
I was terrified because I could not get out of the box.

22
00:01:38.584 --> 00:01:40.205
Then I heard a clanking noise.

23
00:01:40.746 --> 00:01:43.247
My box now seemed to be moving through the waves.

24
00:01:44.027 --> 00:01:45.768
In front of me I could see a ship.

25
00:01:46.569 --> 00:01:49.891
Sailors from the ship had attached a heavy chain to my box.

26
00:01:50.491 --> 00:01:52.252
The ship was towing my box!

27
00:01:52.272 --> 00:01:54.713
"Help! Help!"

28
00:01:55.774 --> 00:01:56.734
I shouted loudly.

29
00:01:57.575 --> 00:01:59.236
I had to make the sailors hear me.

30
00:01:59.888 --> 00:02:02.429
I banged on the wall with my sword as I shouted.

31
00:02:02.449 --> 00:02:03.890
"Who are you?"

32
00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.530
a voice called out.

33
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.712
"I'm Gulliver from England," I cried.

34
00:02:08.732 --> 00:02:11.193
"Please lift the box onto your ship."

35
00:02:12.313 --> 00:02:13.054
I heard laughter.

36
00:02:13.694 --> 00:02:18.896
Someone said, "Even ten men could not lift that box.

37
00:02:19.936 --> 00:02:21.037
He must be crazy!

38
00:02:21.437 --> 00:02:22.518
Let's see who's inside."

39
00:02:23.478 --> 00:02:25.799
A sailor cut a hole in the lid of my box.

40
00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:27.920
"You saved my life!"

41
00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:29.873
I said when I climbed out.

42
00:02:29.893 --> 00:02:31.073
"Thank you!"

43
00:02:32.314 --> 00:02:35.475
I was stunned to see that the sailors were my size.

44
00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:40.017
They asked me many questions and looked at all the things in my box.

45
00:02:40.957 --> 00:02:45.019
A tall man said to me, "Welcome to my ship, the Good Fortune.

46
00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:46.760
I am the captain.

47
00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.821
We are on our way home to England."

48
00:02:49.861 --> 00:02:56.324
"Captain," I said, "I thought I would soon die and never see England or my family again."

49
00:02:57.148 --> 00:02:58.668
"Why were you locked in that box?"

50
00:02:59.249 --> 00:02:59.749
he asked.

51
00:03:00.549 --> 00:03:01.749
"Why was it in the sea?"

52
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:09.632
I told him the whole story—about my voyage on the Adventure and meeting the giants of Brobdingnag.

53
00:03:10.492 --> 00:03:12.072
About Glumdalclitch and the farmer.

54
00:03:12.772 --> 00:03:14.053
About living in the palace.

55
00:03:14.733 --> 00:03:16.053
About my traveling box.

56
00:03:16.073 --> 00:03:23.315
"And I fell asleep in my box on the cliff," I said, "and a huge bird grabbed it,

57
00:03:23.776 --> 00:03:25.156
then dropped it in the sea."

58
00:03:26.552 --> 00:03:29.254
"Get some sleep now," the captain said.

59
00:03:29.955 --> 00:03:31.957
I could tell he did not believe my story.

60
00:03:32.717 --> 00:03:34.859
Later I told him more about Brobdingnag.

61
00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:40.744
I showed him everything in my box, including the huge stingers from the bees I had killed.

62
00:03:41.585 --> 00:03:44.047
When he saw them, he finally believed me.

63
00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:50.353
"I have traveled far," he said, "but I have never seen a land of giants.

64
00:03:51.574 --> 00:03:53.836
How strange and wonderful the world is!"

65
00:03:54.952 --> 00:03:59.416
Months later, in June of 1706, the Good Fortune reached England.

66
00:04:00.337 --> 00:04:02.619
My family was very happy to see me.

67
00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.242
They were amazed when I described my adventures.

68
00:04:06.943 --> 00:04:12.768
"You must promise me," said my wife, "that you will never go to sea again."

69
00:04:13.448 --> 00:04:16.391
For now, my adventures had come to an end.
